Description: relax git → git-man bound from >> to >= for stripped-NMU repo
Author: Harkirat S Virk <harkiratsvirk@gmail.com>
Origin: local
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-05-21
Bug-Athena: git's debian/control declares
   git-man (>> ${source:Upstream-Version}),
   git-man (<< ${source:Upstream-Version}-.)
 which at build time becomes
   Depends: git-man (>> 1:2.39.5), git-man (<< 1:2.39.5-.)
 .
 The idiom relies on Debian's NMU/security suffix to provide the
 strict-greater-than ordering: upstream ships at `1:2.39.5-0+deb12uN`,
 which IS >> 1:2.39.5 because the `+deb12uN` suffix sorts higher than
 the bare upstream string.
 .
 Athena strips NMU suffixes from every package (utils.strip_nmu_from_deb)
 so our git-man ships at the pristine `1:2.39.5-0`.  Per Debian Policy
 §5.6.12 "missing parts shall be treated as if they were '0'", so apt
 considers `1:2.39.5-0` EQUAL to `1:2.39.5` (debrev 0 == missing debrev).
 The `>>` constraint then fails — `apt_pkg.check_dep('1:2.39.5-0', '>>',
 '1:2.39.5')` returns False.  Result: every package_audit run flags
   git Depends: git-man (>> 1:2.39.5) — no satisfying pkg in repo/
 even though the matching git-man IS in repo at the matching version.
 .
 Fix: relax the lower bound to `>=`.  The matching upper bound
 `<< 1:2.39.5-.` still prevents accepting any wrong-major-version
 git-man (`.` sorts higher than any digit, so this rejects 1:2.39.5-99
 etc); the `>=` lower bound now accepts our bare-debrev `1:2.39.5-0`
 while still rejecting older 2.38.x.
 .
 TEMPORARY: revisit when CONF-08 lands or we add a security-update
 bump layer that brings the strict-greater-than ordering back.
---
This patch header follows DEP-3: http://dep.debian.net/deps/dep3/
--- a/debian/control
+++ b/debian/control
@@ -28,7 +28,7 @@
 Architecture: any
 Multi-Arch: foreign
 Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, perl, liberror-perl,
- git-man (>> ${source:Upstream-Version}), git-man (<< ${source:Upstream-Version}-.)
+ git-man (>= ${source:Upstream-Version}), git-man (<< ${source:Upstream-Version}-.)
 Pre-Depends: ${misc:Pre-Depends}
 Recommends: ca-certificates, patch, less, ssh-client
 Suggests: gettext-base, git-daemon-run | git-daemon-sysvinit,
